xpected": false, "id": "contract-49237", "intent": "How can I add a period to a cell in Excel if there is a middle initial present, and leave it blank if there is no middle initial? The middle initial is obtained from the full name in cell E19 with first name in E5 and last name in E7. The extraction formula I'm using for the middle name is `=TRIM(MID(E19,LEN(E5)+1,LEN(E19)-LEN(E5&E7)))`, which gives the middle name in E9. Then I'm converting it to proper case with `=PROPER(E9)` in F10, and I'm taking the initial from that result with `=LEFT(F10)` in F7. If F7 contains an initial, I want to add a period after it. Otherwise, F7 should remain blank. Every formula I've tried results in a `#VALUE` error. What formula should I use to achieve this?", "invariants": ["workbook remains structurally valid", "Preserve all existing data, formulas, and formatting in cells outside Sheet1!F7."], "required_capabilities": [{"name": "write_cells", "version": "1.0.0"}, {"name": "recalculate", "version": "1.0.0"}, {"name": "validate_workbook", "version": "1.0.0"}], "version": 2, "visual_intent": false}}, "sequence": 1, "timestamp_unix": 1788679202.960876}
